# Date values

Follow the project skill `.agents/skills/add-date-value/SKILL.md`. Design notes: `docs/structured-date-model.md`.

- Types, `Validate` and `CompactDisplay` live in `core/datevalue`; use `datevalues.Insert` / `Lookup` for storage; an owner (an Observation, a Source) stores its date through `datevalues.PutTx` (edit in place, audited) and releases a replaced one through `deleteimpact.ReleaseReplaced`; where a date sorts is `valuecompare.DateKeyOf` / `DateKey.Compare`, the one date order; kinds `point` / `range`; point qualifiers `ABT` / `BEF` / `AFT`.
- The Person page's Timeline starts from it and moves a row only where the dates cannot say which came first (`persondetail` `lifelineTypes.order`, `structured-date-model.md` § 3.4); that is not a sort, and no other list moves rows.
- Optional civil components (gaps allowed); at least one of year/month/day/hour/minute/second or a phrase; free-text `start_tz` / `end_tz`; empty = unspecified (not UTC).
- Schema changes go through catalog migrations; do not invent a parallel date store.
